A struct marshalled as JSON by a function nothing calls: the sweep finds every
field of it dead under reachability, and the encoding-reflection class retains the
exported one, which is the shape that puts a written declaration in the retained
record rather than in the candidate set.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/wire

go 1.27.1
-- main.go --
package main

import "encoding/json"

// answer is written out as JSON, which reads every exported field of it.
type answer struct {
	Status string `json:"status"`
	note   string
}

// reply sets both fields and marshals the answer. Nothing calls it.
func reply() ([]byte, error) {
	a := answer{}
	a.Status = "ok"
	a.note = "unread"
	return json.Marshal(a)
}

func main() {}
